.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt PEM_READ_BIO_EX 3ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm PEM_read_bio_ex ,
.Nm PEM_FLAG_SECURE ,
.Nm PEM_FLAG_EAY_COMPATIBLE ,
.Nm PEM_FLAG_ONLY_B64
.Nd read PEM format files with custom processing
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In openssl/pem.h
.Fd #define PEM_FLAG_SECURE             0x1
.Fd #define PEM_FLAG_EAY_COMPATIBLE     0x2
.Fd #define PEM_FLAG_ONLY_B64           0x4
.Ft int
.Fo PEM_read_bio_ex
.Fa "BIO *in"
.Fa "char **name"
.Fa "char **header"
.Fa "unsigned char **data"
.Fa "long *len"
.Fa "unsigned int flags"
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn PEM_read_bio_ex
reads in PEM formatted data from an input BIO, outputting the name of
the type of contained data, the header information regarding the
possibly encrypted data, and the binary data payload (after base64
decoding).
It should generally only be used to implement PEM_read_bio_-family
functions for specific data types or other usage, but is exposed to
allow greater flexibility over how processing is performed, if needed.
.Pp
If
.Dv PEM_FLAG_SECURE
is set, the intermediate buffers used to read in lines of input are
allocated from the secure heap.
.Pp
If
.Dv PEM_FLAG_EAY_COMPATIBLE
is set, a simple algorithm is used to remove whitespace and control
characters from the end of each line, so as to be compatible with the
historical behavior of
.Xr PEM_read_bio 3 .
.Pp
If
.Dv PEM_FLAG_ONLY_B64
is set, all characters are required to be valid base64 characters (or
newlines); non-base64 characters are treated as end of input.
.Pp
If neither
.Dv PEM_FLAG_EAY_COMPATIBLE
or
.Dv PEM_FLAG_ONLY_B64
is set, control characters are ignored.
.Pp
If both
.Dv PEM_FLAG_EAY_COMPATIBLE
and
.Dv PEM_FLAG_ONLY_B64
are set, an error is returned; these options are not compatible with
each other.
.Sh NOTES
The caller must release the storage allocated for *name, *header, and
*data.
If
.Dv PEM_FLAG_SECURE
was set, use
.Xr OPENSSL_secure_free 3 ;
otherwise,
.Xr OPENSSL_free 3
is used.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn PEM_read_bio_ex
returns 1 for success or 0 for failure.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr PEM_bytes_read_bio 3
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Fn PEM_read_bio_ex
function was added in OpenSSL 1.1.1.
